{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAt RED the gate still"}
{"type":"thought","data":" defines its own functions"}
{"type":"thought","data":" inline, so --self-check"}
{"type":"thought","data":" may pass without the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" identity module. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" test expects FAIL policy-import"}
{"type":"thought","data":" at RED to be F because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that behavior does "}
{"type":"thought","data":"not yet exist."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe test failure at"}
{"type":"thought","data":" RED is an assertion"}
{"type":"thought","data":" mismatch, not an error."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Even if --self-check"}
{"type":"thought","data":" crashes with a traceback"}
{"type":"thought","data":" when importing the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"missing identity module,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the test still fails"}
{"type":"thought","data":" because it expects "}
{"type":"thought","data":"a specific stderr line."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nTask 55's mutation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" row `fr6-import-guard-dropped`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" replaces a guarded "}
{"type":"thought","data":"import with a bare one."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The corresponding test"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" runs against a gate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" copied beside a judge"}
{"type":"thought","data":" without the identity"}
{"type":"thought","data":" module."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nA bare top-level import"}
{"type":"thought","data":" raises ModuleNotFoundError"}
{"type":"thought","data":" before main, producing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exit 1 and no JSON."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The test expects kind=judge-error"}
{"type":"thought","data":" JSON, so the failure"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is expected.\n\nThe next"}
{"type":"thought","data":" step is to grep the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" working directory for"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the implementation "}
{"type":"thought","data":"plan, design file, mutation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" counts, Record class,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" STATE_ACTIVE_RE, merge_fields"}
{"type":"thought","data":" signature, production"}
{"type":"thought","data":" paths needing red tests,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and hook_wiring rows."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe grep targets now"}
{"type":"thought","data":" include specific implementation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" details: CX-FOLD and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CX-FORCE-SCRIPT constants,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the codex self-check"}
{"type":"thought","data":" FAIL parser, canonical"}
{"type":"thought","data":" empty target handling,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" M-2 row counts, ACTIVE_RE,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" JUDGE_BUDGET_S, TIMEOUT"}
{"type":"thought","data":" defaults, docstring"}
{"type":"thought","data":" line 50, agent choices,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" heartbeat anchors, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"class (b) tools, agy-runtime"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SessionStart, prompt"}
{"type":"thought","data":" opening line, failure-recovery"}
{"type":"thought","data":" context sentences, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"git SHA 4e4b5ded versus"}
{"type":"thought","data":" HEAD, HemaSuite reference,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" fr3 probe mode, test_codex_hook_self_check,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" KINDS count, _deny "}
{"type":"thought","data":"count, and schema properties"}
{"type":"thought","data":" order. The plan itself may be embedded in "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the prompt rather than"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a separate file, so"}
{"type":"thought","data":" TBD, TODO, and FIXME"}
{"type":"thought","data":" markers should also"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be checked.\n\nTask 20's amendment"}
{"type":"thought","data":" supersedes the six-tool"}
{"type":"thought","data":" scope but leaves the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" acceptance criteria"}
{"type":"thought","data":" unchanged, so the old"}
{"type":"thought","data":" requirements remain"}
{"type":"thought","data":" normative. The design"}
{"type":"thought","data":" still lists the FAIL"}
{"type":"thought","data":" parser as owed, yet"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the implementation "}
{"type":"thought","data":"plan fixes it, satisfying"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that design item without"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a plan bug. The design"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Test Plan also cites"}
{"type":"thought","data":" test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for AC-2.1 and AC-2.2."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan diverges "}
{"type":"thought","data":"from the design on AC-3.2"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and justifies the difference."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The property_valid "}
{"type":"thought","data":"dict guard row is correctly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" placed in Task 1 under"}
{"type":"thought","data":" FR-7, consistent with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the plan's rule to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"place rows near their"}
{"type":"thought","data":" code. The design v1.4"}
{"type":"thought","data":" row count of nineteen"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is accurate: four in"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Task 5, eleven in Task"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 6, and four in Task"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 7.\n\nI am manually counting"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the design's FR-4 mutation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bullets to verify the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan's claim of nineteen"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rows. The first ten"}
{"type":"thought","data":" items are being tallied"}
{"type":"thought","data":" now."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe manual count of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" design FR-4 mutation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bullets is complete"}
{"type":"thought","data":" at nineteen. The plan's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" four Task 5 rows are"}
{"type":"thought","data":" discipline, class-a-name-moved,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" class-d-default-allows,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" finally-deny-dropped,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and step5-s-dropped."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design's FR-4 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"mutation count is confirmed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" at nineteen. Task 6"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contains eleven rows"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and Task 7 contains"}
{"type":"thought","data":" four.\n\nA discrepancy"}
{"type":"thought","data":" was found for the empty-string"}
{"type":"thought","data":" active target killer:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the design uses `\"\"`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" while the plan uses"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `number-inactive` and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `list-inactive`."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan corrects "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the design's fixture,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" so the discrepancy "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is not a plan defect."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The non-empty-str mutant"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is properly discriminated:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" truthy non-string values"}
{"type":"thought","data":" like 5 trigger TypeError"}
{"type":"thought","data":" in canonicalise, while"}
{"type":"thought","data":" inactive targets correctly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" allow."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nTask 6 item 1's RED"}
{"type":"thought","data":" split is verified: "}
{"type":"thought","data":"six nodes are P and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"four are F. Unknown "}
{"type":"thought","data":"nodes are no-key-unknown"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and empty-unknown. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Inactive nodes are no-key-inactive,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" empty-inactive, number-inactive,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and list-inactive. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Active nodes are empty-active,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" null-active, number-active,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and list-active."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe null-active node"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is confirmed as F at"}
{"type":"thought","data":" RED because class (d)"}
{"type":"thought","data":" denies tool-not-admitted"}
{"type":"thought","data":" under active, causing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the judge-error assertion"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to fail. The next step"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is to audit the tree"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for factual errors "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and re-examine Task "}
{"type":"thought","data":"9's nine-row claim and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" other count bugs."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nTask 3 claims 56 hook"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rows and 40 judge rows."}
{"type":"thought","data":" M-2 lists 56 hook specs"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and 8 judge specs. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Task 2 adds one implementer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" spec, bringing the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"total to 12 judge specs."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The listed names match"}
{"type":"thought","data":" this count."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nHook specs may overlap"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with judge specs, so"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the union of 12 is not simply 8 plus 5. Task 10's claim of 60 assembler rows matches M-2's 6 specs. Task 4 cites git SHA 84ec2133 for the codex gate, but the plan indicates the tree is at 4e4b5ded and h-mad has not changed since a8d9ba99."}
