ion\": \"Optional Codex availability declaration; absent/null means available. Phase-5 authoring is resolved by h_mad_tdd_judge.py implementer using both Codex and agy availability. Codex being out alone does not permit Claude to author: fallback_agent is read only when both peers are out. The orchestrator separately uses unavailable/exhausted to route the second audit surface; that routing is prose-enforced by SKILL.md, not read automatically by the audit script. Set back to available when Codex returns.\","},{"line_number":153,"content":"    \"fallback_agent\": {"},{"line_number":154,"content":"      \"description\": \"Who covers Phase-5 authoring when both peers are out. The field is read only when codex is out and agy is out too: each peer is out when its HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE/HMAD_AGY_UNAVAILABLE flag is non-empty, its codex_status/agy_status is unavailable|exhausted, or its CLI is not on PATH. Absent, null and 'claude' are equivalent: Claude covers, test-first. HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE does not override 'grok'; a one-off Claude escape needs --set fallback_agent=claude. Audit-leg routing to grok (audit-cycle --surfaces agy,grok) is prose-enforced by SKILL.md, and no script reads this field for it.\","}]}]},"locations":[]}
